# Cloudflare Pages headers.
#
# DEC-436 (2026-07-03 security audit, SEC-1): global security headers. Nothing
# legitimate embeds TripPilot in an iframe, so denying framing kills clickjacking
# on every route — including the guest pages /s/:id and /g/:id which show
# balances. Deliberately NO full CSP (script-src/style-src) here: the app relies
# on inline styles + Google Fonts, so a strict CSP needs its own tested wave.
# Permissions-Policy must keep geolocation/microphone/camera enabled for self —
# the app uses GPS stamping, voice entry and receipt capture.
/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(self), microphone=(self), camera=(self)
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains

# DEC-206 fix: the native app runs at https://localhost (androidScheme: 'https'),
# so its fetch of the version manifest on this host is cross-origin. Without an
# Access-Control-Allow-Origin header the WebView blocks the response, the app can
# never see a newer bundle, and the OTA self-update never fires. Allowing any
# origin on the manifest (and the OTA bundles) unblocks the live-update check.
/version.json
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Cache-Control: no-store

/bundles/*
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
